ethods data analysis procedures</article-title><source>TQR</source><year>2006</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>474</fpage><lpage>98</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dub&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Teng</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hawkins</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaplow</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Savage GT, Blair JD, Fottler MD</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Emotions, the neglected side of patient-centered health care management: The case of emergency department patients waiting to see a physician</article-title><source>Advances in Health Care Management</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Oxford: Elsevier Science</publisher-name><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>193</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kristiansen</surname><given-names>IS</given-names></name><name><surname>Forde</surname><given-names>OH</given-names></name><name><surname>Aasland</surname><given-names>OG</given-names></name><name><surname>Hotvedt</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnsen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Forde</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Threats from patients and their effects on medical decision making: a cross-sectional, randomized trial</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2001</year><volume>357</volume><fpage>1258</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11418151</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Allan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Finucane</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A 30-month study of patient complaints at a major Australian hospital</article-title><source>J Qual Clin Pract</source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>109</fpage><lpage>111</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11856405</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lammers</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Duggan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bringing the physician back in: Communication predictors of physicians' satisfaction with managed care</article-title><source>Health Commun</source><year>2002</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>493</fpage><lpage>513</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12375773</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Veldhuis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Defensive behaviour of Dutch family physicians. Widening the concept</article-title><source>Fam Med</source><year>1994</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>29</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8132141</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Continuing Professional Development of Physicians: From Research to Practice</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Chicago: American Medical Association</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Matern</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Koneczny</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Safety, hazards and ergonomics in the operating room</article-title><source>Surg Endosc</source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1965</fpage><lpage>1969</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17483989</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Keely</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Dojeiji</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Byszewski</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Marks</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Communication skills, cultural challenges and individual support: Challenges of international medical graduates in a Canadian healthcare environment</article-title><source>Med Teach</source><year>2004</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>120</fpage><lpage>125</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15203520</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O'Neale Roach</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Guthrie</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dealing with stress: Medical schools should teach us how to cope</article-title><source>student BMJ</source><year>2000</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>218</fpage><lpage>219</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Carrera</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Stratton</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Bickel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nora</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Experiences of belittlement and harassment and their correlates among medical students in the United States</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2006</year><volume>333</volume><fpage>682</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16956894</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Patten</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Wellbeing in residency training: A survey examining resident physician satisfaction both within and outside of residency training and mental health in Alberta</article-title><source>BMC Med Educ</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>21</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15972100</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cheema</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Naqvi</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Giri</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaliaperumal</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bullying of junior doctors prevails in Irish health system: A bitter reality</article-title><source>Ir Med J</source><year>2005</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>274</fpage><lpage>275</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16300107</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Brogan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Schiffman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevalence and correlates of harassment among U.S. women physicians</article-title><source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>158</volume><fpage>352</fpag